site: drop four Wix carryover pages the landing page never claimed

A first pass over pages that came across from Wix and were never sculpted into the new site. Each
one here either said what the footer already says, or existed separately only because Wix had a
separate URL for it. Nothing is lost: wix.fcpublicmedia.local holds the snapshot.

- `/book/` → `/reserve/`. Both rendered the same "not wired up yet" notice for the same room
  request; `/reserve/` is the one in the header menu. Its waiting-for-a-reply copy moves there.
- `/register/` → `/classes/`. Same, for the same class signup. `/classes/` is "Learn" in the menu.
- `/teach/` → `/classes/#teach-with-us`. A TODO asking for the instructor application's questions,
  on a page whose only inbound link was the sentence on `/classes/` pointing at it.
- `/bulletin-board/` → dropped. The Wix page embedded Cablecast CG's bulletin board
  (`machines/broadcast/PROFILE.md`), which is the channel's own between-programs page and is
  already ejected as slides and rendered on ch97 standby. `/community-bulletin-board` now goes to
  `/watch/`.

No `from` leaves `redirects.yml`; five are retargeted. `_includes/request-form.html` and
`_data/forms.yml` had no other reader and go with the two request pages.

Merge qualifications:
- [x] `bundle exec jekyll build` clean
- [x] Playwright `--grep-invert @external`: 553 passed, 1 skipped, 0 failed
- [x] token, secret and internal-publish tests pass
- [x] no internal link in `_site` resolves to a dropped page
- [x] every Wix `from` still has a built target

Left standing, named for a second pass: `/about/`, `/contact/`, `/nonprofits/`,
`/policies/non-discrimination/`.

